  "text": "DES K6 (Part 2 section 10.3), written before the simulation runs: if the simulated familywise rate exceeds 6% at any simulated sigma, SR-2 is not adopted and N decides alone; else SR-2 stands and the size is printed. GXB S-1: the rule applies to every simulated scenario: a familywise rate above 6% at any simulated sigma, with or without the interaction and at either family ratio (every entry of 'interaction'; GXB R-12), and for any family read, means SR-2 is not adopted. It runs before block A's first pod, on the design that will run (the reduced design if an anchor-job stop is known before it runs; DESO3 V2; GXB S-10). The script prints this rule and a reading line beside its largest familywise rate over every sigma, scenario and family; the lead applies it. The familywise rate is the rate of the U claims (Holm on U at 5%; Part 2 section 10.3); Phi's O and L words are not simulated (GXB R-11).",
